<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="de">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Markdown-Liste</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #0e0f12;
      --text: #d6d9df;
      --muted: #8b90a0;
      --accent: #9aa5ff;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 2rem;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", monospace;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    h1, h2, h3 {
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    }

    h1::before { content: "# "; color: var(--muted); }
    h2::before { content: "## "; color: var(--muted); }
    h3::before { content: "### "; color: var(--muted); }

    ul {
      list-style: none;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
    }

    li::before {
      content: "- ";
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-left: -1.5rem;
    }

    li {
      margin: 0.25rem 0;
    }

    p {
      color: var(--text);
      margin: 0.5rem 0;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Meine Liste</h1>

  <ul>
    <li>Erster Punkt</li>
    <li>Zweiter Punkt</li>
    <li>Dritter Punkt</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Notizen</h2>

  <p>Das fühlt sich an wie Markdown, ist aber pures HTML.</p>

</body>
</html>
